{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeClausenWitness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeClausenWitness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingBringZeroMode","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.CatalanClausenBridge","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Real.Pi.Bounds"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass.bring_zero_mode_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass.bring_zero_mode_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeRootOfUnityClass","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean#L63-L71","doc":"**Corrected statement (conjecture, no instance).**  The content the class\ndocstring intends: the angle is a rational multiple of `π`, i.e. the Bloch\nclass has a root-of-unity shape.  For such `θ`, `Cl₂(θ)` is an `L`-value\ncombination, and `Cl₂(θ) = 2/(3π)` would make `π · Cl₂(θ)` rational, which\nis expected to fail; no proof either way is known.  Per §3b-cond there is\nno instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.exists_Cl_2_eq_bringZeroModeValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.exists_Cl_2_eq_bringZeroModeValue","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean#L47-L61","doc":"**The Clausen witness.**  There is `θ ∈ [0, π/2]` with\n`Cl₂(θ) = 2/(3π)`, by the intermediate value theorem between\n`Cl₂(0) = 0` and `Cl₂(π/2) = G > 0.915`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroModeValue_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroModeValue_pos","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean#L44-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroModeValue_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroModeValue_lt","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringZeroModeClausenWitness.lean#L37-L42","doc":"`2/(3π) < 2/9`, from `π > 3`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}